    "media:imagetext": "-2.\n$1,250,000 cash with no strings attached. It was, of course,\nin view of the State Department's stand, the one course left\nopen to us.\nBond made a wonderful deal under all the cir-\ncumstances and PAA got the money on December 30th.\nAt Hongkong the British refused to recognize the sale\neven though it was made by\nthe then British-recognized gov-\nernment of China and covered\nproperty which was legally theirs\nto dispose of as they wished.\nThe whole question of title to\nthe aircraft is now before the Hongkong court. Meanwhile, the\nBritish have recognized the Communist government.\nThe airport\nis covered with airplanes and the only flying is being done by\nswarms of buzzard-like lawyers waiting to swoop down on any\nclaim which appears vulnerable.\nI stayed in Hongkong only two days and then came up\nhere after making arrangements for Debby and Hebe to get hotel\nspace from February 10th to 16th in the Colony. We felt they\nshould leave Bangkok before the big meeting of diplomats which\nwill be held there starting February 13th as hotel accommodations\nin Bangkok are both scarce and sub-standard.\nHaving spent a few deys in India enroute here I feel\nas well qualified as most experts to discuss the India-Pakistan\nYou know what was formeriy India, a piece of pie-\nshaped land, is now divided very roughly by a wide strip down\nfrom the broad top to either side of the point, and that section\nis called India.\nIt takes in Calcutta on the east and Bombay\non the west but does not include Karadhi which is the capital\nof Pakistan.\nThe small sections on either side of this wide\nstrip are called East Pakistan and West Pakistan.\nThe citizens\nof the latter country are Moslems while the Indians are Hindus.\nSuch is the hatred of the one for the other that there can be\nno peace between them.\nBoth claimed the erstwhile independent\nHyderabad, the ruler of which wes Moslem but the big majority\nof the people were Hindus; Pandit Nehru took Hyderabad by force\nof arms but he contends with respect to the only large inde-\npendent state left (i.e. Kashinir) that India must have that,\ntoo although the situation in Kashmir is exactly the reverse\nof Hyderabad only in this instance the ruler of Kashmir is a\nHindu and the people are probably 80% Moslem.\nApparently\namong politicians - no matter how elevated their speeches -\nconsistency is not a virtue.\nThe pity of the whole thing is that both countries\nare spending the largest part of their national income on war\nmeterial\nand military establishments. Another tragic con-\nsequence is that Pakistan is more than self-sufficient on food-\nstuff while thousands of Indiens are starving. Nevertheless,\nPakistan is exporting wheat to Europe while its neighbor\nIndia is importing wheat from Australia.\nFurthermore, Pakistan\nhas large dollar receipts from the sale of long staple cotton,\nwheat, hides, jute and minerals while India must import many\nof these products in order to run its industriel plants, but\nPakistan won't sell to them. India has a population of",
